\begin_layout Standard
Bioconductor has served as the gold standard for high-throughput genomic analysis by providing standardized data structures and reproducible statistical methods,
 whereas Python has quickly become the primary environment for deep learning,
 image analysis,
 and general-purpose data science.
 This presents a challenge to the scientific community by forcing them to navigating complex,
 fragile,
 and often inefficient interoperability solutions to leverage the strengths of both worlds.
 We present BiocPy,
 a software framework and ecosystem designed to bridge this gap by reengineering the foundational Bioconductor data structures as native Python data representations.
 BiocPy provides Python-native implementations that adhere to Bioconductor’s S4 class semantics,
 including ingestion of serialized R data objects.
 This approach allows developers to build robust,
 polyglot workflows that leverage the strengths of both ecosystems without compromising data integrity.
 All packages in the BiocPy ecosystem are published to Python's Package Index (PyPI) and code available on GitHub at 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
target "http://github.com/BiocPy"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

