\begin_layout Section
Discussion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
While BiocPy provides a bridge between ecosystems,
 we acknowledge current limitations relative to the mature Bioconductor project.
 First,
 BiocPy focuses on foundational data structures and core single-cell analysis workflows;
 it does not yet mirror (nor is our intent) the vast repository of over 2,000 specialized packages available in R.
 Finally,
 while rds2py enables efficient data ingestion,
 it currently supports core classes;
 highly custom user-defined S4 objects may require additional configuration for mapping.
 BiocPy provides the necessary structure for stable and sustainable software development.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
biocpy helps bioconductor developers write similar packages in python.
 the aim is to provide a familiar core representations.
 we don't support all bioconductor classes yet but we are working towards it.
 we are working on extending to spatial.
 we don't mirror the analysis methods,
 we aim to make it easier for other developers to make equivalent and facilitate the translation.
\end_layout

